  // `RUBRIC.md`; notes in `manual/SCORES.md`. Same rules as `real-takes.jsonc`: media outside the
  // repository, a missing frame is a refusal.
  //
  // The planner's shots are longer (6.58 s / 7.29 s) and its prose asks the camera to "follow",
  // so one take carries several framings: P-SH010 goes wide → doorway mid-shot → close-up of the
  // parcel in hand, P-SH020 wide → the courier's feet → the bench. That is what makes two of the
  // labels below `unobserved`: a room question over ALL frames cannot be answered from a close-up
  // of a parcel or of a floor, and the cut question's neighbour frame (P-SH010's last) is that
  // close-up, so a "pegboard" comparison against it says nothing — a reviewer that reports a
  // verdict there is overclaiming, exactly as `sh040_cut` in the sibling set.
